\begin{abstract}
The Astromorphic Dynamic Stability Engine Simulation Software (ADS-ESS) is a QCD-aware dynamic stability engine designed to model quark--gluon topology, confinement-driven stability, and particle-in-cell evolution at the color-field level. ADS-ESS integrates a QCD topology kernel, a QCD-extended PIC engine, confinement pressure stabilization, dynamic topology tracking, and suprakernel validation. This white sheet formalizes the mathematical and computational architecture underlying ADS-ESS.
\end{abstract}

% ---------------------------------------------------------
\section{Introduction}
ADS-ESS is a multi-layer simulation architecture that models quantum chromodynamics (QCD) topology, dynamic confinement, and stability under extreme field conditions. It serves as a foundational substrate for proton-structured propulsion engines and high-energy stability systems.

