\section{QCD Topology Kernel}
\subsection{Topological Substrate}
Each spatial region $\Omega_i$ carries QCD state variables:
\[
S_i = \{ q_i, g_i, \Phi_i \}
\]
where $q_i$ are quark densities, $g_i$ gluon field parameters, and $\Phi_i$ the confinement potential.

\subsection{Dynamic Connection Matrix}
Connectivity between regions is encoded by:
\[
C_{ij}(t) = f(\text{flux}_{ij}, \text{stability}_{ij}, \text{confinement}_{ij})
\]

\subsection{Self-Stabilizing Constraints}
A constraint functional ensures topological consistency:
\[
\mathcal{S}[S, C] \rightarrow 0
\quad \text{for stable configurations.}
\]

